# 40. Git Reset – Day 25

## Soft

```bash
git reset --soft <commit>
```

Moves `HEAD` but keeps changes staged.

## Mixed

```bash
git reset --mixed <commit>
```

Moves `HEAD` and unstages changes while keeping working-directory changes.

This is the default:

```bash
git reset <commit>
```

## Hard

```bash
git reset --hard <commit>
```

Moves `HEAD` and resets the staging area and tracked working-directory changes.

### Quick Comparison

| Reset     | Commit | Staging   | Working Directory |
| --------- | ------ | --------- | ----------------- |
| `--soft`  | Reset  | Preserved | Preserved         |
| `--mixed` | Reset  | Reset     | Preserved         |
| `--hard`  | Reset  | Reset     | Reset             |

> ⚠️ `--hard` can permanently discard uncommitted tracked changes.

