# 41. Git Revert – Day 25

```bash
git revert <commit-hash>
```

`git revert` creates a **new commit** that reverses the changes introduced by another commit.

### Reset vs Revert

|               | `git reset`         | `git revert`                   |
| ------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Purpose       | Move branch pointer | Undo changes with a new commit |
| History       | Can rewrite history | Preserves existing history     |
| Shared branch | Risky               | Safer                          |
| Typical use   | Local/private work  | Shared/pushed work             |

### Easy Memory Trick

```text
RESET  → Rewrite / move history
REVERT → New commit that undoes changes
```

