# 49. Common Linux Text-Processing Pipeline

One of the most useful Linux patterns is:

```text
Command
   ↓
 grep
   ↓
 awk
   ↓
 sort
   ↓
 uniq
   ↓
 head
```

Example:

```bash
grep "ERROR" app.log |
awk '{print $NF}' |
sort |
uniq -c |
sort -rn |
head -5
```

### General Pattern

```text
Inspect → Filter → Extract → Sort → Count → Interpret
```

